'' RUN: abort( ) under -exx is runtime error 14 -- the message and the exit code fbc-modern
'' gives. TK-004 changed how the signal handler gets there (it peeks the thread's error context
'' and never allocates, since glibc may abort from inside malloc), not what it prints.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/signal-abort.bas -o tests/codegen/signalabort.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/signalabort.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 14
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: before
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Aborting due to runtime error 14 ("abnormal termination" signal) in tests/codegen/src/signal-abort.bas::()
